gives Ledbetter the opportunity to record proof of Casey's shenanigans. On the sidelines, the Tackleberrys care for an infant left at their door.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":10,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1997-10-13\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":5,\"name\":\"Dead Man Talking\",\"overview\":\"A photographer with incriminating evidence is brought to the Academy for protection. Meanwhile, District Attorney Callahan has eyes for Commandant Hefilfinger.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-10-20\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":6,\"name\":\"Mummy Dearest\",\"overview\":\"The Commandant was delivered an Egyptian mummy by a delivery mistake for his exercise bicycle. Meanwhile, Annie pretends to be a drill instructor in attempt to impress her strict father.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-10-27\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":7,\"name\":\"No Sweat, Sweet\",\"overview\":\"An over-the-hill boxer enrols in the Academy to toughen up. Meanwhile, Casey must find out who has been stealing the cadets' personal belongings.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-11-03\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":8,\"name\":\"All At Sea\",\"overview\":\"While on a beach stakeout, Casey becomes involved with an attractive TV star who is kidnapped. Meanwhile, Annie fears she may be cursed, and visits a psychic for assistance.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-11-10\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":9,\"name\":\"Les Is More\",\"overview\":\"Casey is stalked by a woman obsessed with marrying him, just as romance is blossoming between Casey and Annie. Meanwhile, Lester develops multiple-personality disorder after a knock to the head.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-11-17\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":10,\"name\":\"If I Were A Rich Cop\",\"overview\":\"Casey finds an ancient journal with clues to a buried treasure on Academy grounds. In a misunderstanding issue, Annie is upset when Casey cheats on his written assignment.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-11-24\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":11,\"name\":\"Shopping with the Enemy\",\"overview\":\"With the cancellation of summer vacation, Hefilfinger and the cadets try to get their Christmas shopping in early, but find themselves held captive by a group of inept thugs.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1997-12-01\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":12,\"name\":\"Luke....Warm\",\"overview\":\"Annie has a secret admirer in Luke, but the feeling is not quite mutual. Meanwhile, the Tackleberrys are hot on the trail of some missing squad car\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-01-26\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":13,\"name\":\"The Truth Ain't What It Used To Be\",\"overview\":\"Police Academy court is in session. With Hefilfinger as judge, and Ledbetter as prosecutor, Casey is put on trial for allegedly assisting a bank robber.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-02-02\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Hoop Nightmares\",\"overview\":\"In an attempt to raise money for Annie's surprise birthday party, Casey bets on the annual basketball game between the Academy's and Sheriff's cadets.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-02-09\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"Lend Me Your Ears\",\"overview\":\"Eric Lassard comes out of retirement to fill in as Commandant, while Hefilfinger takes a refresher course. Meanwhile, Ledbetter experiments with a new hair-growth treatment.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-02-16\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"Dr. Hightower\",\"overview\":\"Captain Hightower returns to the Academy to train the new cadets, and to receive an award as \\\"Alumnus of the Year\\\", while also lending Casey a helping hand in tracking down an armored car thief.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-02-23\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"Bring Me the Turtle of Commandant Hefilfinger\",\"overview\":\"The Commandant's pet turtle, Zeus, becomes possessed by a creature from outer space. Meanwhile, Ledbetter attempts an Academy takeover while Lester teams up with Cassandra to catch a thief on the sidelines.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-03-02\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":18,\"name\":\"Karate Cops\",\"overview\":\"The cadets are led to a couple of jewel thieves, after Commandant Hefilfinger finds a ruby in his fortune cookie.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-03-30\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":19,\"name\":\"A Horse Of Course\",\"overview\":\"When Lester's new equestrianism friend gets kidnapped, it's up to Casey and the cadets to find and return the horse to its rightful owner.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-04-06\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":20,\"name\":\"Mr. I.Q.\",\"overview\":\"Lester joins a dating service, using Casey's photo on his profile. Jones tutors the cadets on how to detect a pickpocket. Luke becomes a game show contestant.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-04-13\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":21,\"name\":\"Team Tack\",\"overview\":\"Captain Tackleberry is set up for blackmail by the owner of a strip club after Tack shuts them down. Meanwhile, Ledbetter orders Casey to help Luke lose weight.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1998-04-20\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":22,\"name\":\"Cadet of the Year\",\"overview\":\"Hefilfinger organises a Cadet of the Year competition to increase the number of Academy enlistments, but Ledbetter does his best to keep Casey from winning. Furthermor due to budget cuts, Commissioner Hurst is named the new Commandant.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":9,\"voteCount\":1,\"airDate\":\"1998-04-27\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":23,\"name\":\"Got Insurance?\",\"overview\":\"Casey tries to defend the Academy against the shady lawyer of the Academy's janitor, who files a lawsuit after Luke accidentally injures him.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-05-04\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":24,\"name\":\"Angel On My Back\",\"overview\":\"Ledbetter meets his guardian angel, who warns him to start treating his cadets with compassion or suffer the consequences.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-05-11\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":25,\"name\":\"Lend Me Your Neck\",\"overview\":\"Annie is stalked by a mental patient who thinks he is a vampire. Meanwhile, a woman turns up at the Academy, claiming to be Hefilfinger's daughter.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-05-18\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":26,\"name\":\"Rich No More\",\"overview\":\"Ledbetter and the cadets embark on a ski trip for winter break. Alice & Annie have the hots for a handsome concierge. The Tackleberrys try befriending Lester. Casey meets the love of his life, but has trouble being accepted by her father.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1998-05-25\",\"runtime\":60}],\"firstAirDate\":\"1997-09-22\"}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":86400,"tags":[]}